We can now craft final answer with routes and include the stadium as optional. Provide details.assistantfinal## 🎯  Three Ready‑to‑Go Tour Routes in Madrid  
Below are three themed itineraries that string together the most‑visited attractions (the “trending” attractions the API returned for **Madrid**).  For each stop I’ve included the key details the API gave you – description, address, opening hours, ticket price, a quick tip, and a highlight you won’t want to miss.

---

## 1️⃣ Classic Madrid – “Royal & Historic Highlights”

| Time (approx.) | Attraction | What to See / Do | API‑Provided Details |
|----------------|------------|------------------|----------------------|
| **09:00 – 11:00** | **Royal Palace of Madrid** (`royal-palace-madrid`) | • Grand staircases, Throne Room, Royal Armoury  <br>• Optional audio‑guide tour | **Address:** Calle de Bailén, 28071 Madrid, Spain  <br>**Opening:** 10:00‑20:00 (Apr‑Oct) / 10:00‑18:00 (Nov‑Mar)  <br>**Ticket:** €13 (adult) – free for EU citizens 65+  <br>**Tip:** Arrive right at opening to beat the security line; the palace gardens are free and perfect for a quick photo. |
| **11:30 – 13:00** | **Plaza Mayor** (public square) | • 17‑arcade historic market <br>• Street‑performers, cafés, Statue of Philip III | **Address:** Plaza Mayor, 28012 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** Open 24 h (public space)  <br>**Tip:** Grab a *bocadillo de calamares* at a nearby bar for a true Madrid snack. |
| **13:30 – 15:00** | **Lunch – Mercado de San Miguel** (food hall) | • Tapas, fresh seafood, Iberian ham, local wines | **Address:** Plaza de San Miguel, 28005 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 10:00‑24:00  <br>**Tip:** Try the *paella* and a glass of sherry; it’s a 5‑minute walk from Plaza Mayor. |
| **15:30 – 18:00** | **Museo del Prado** (`prado-museum`) | • Masterpieces by Velázquez, Goya, El Greco, Bosch  <br>• Temporary “Spanish Baroque” exhibition | **Address:** Calle de Felipe IV, s/n, 28014 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 10:00‑20:00 (Mon‑Sat) / 10:00‑19:00 (Sun)  <br>**Ticket:** €15 (adult) – free after 18:00 on weekdays  <br>**Highlights:** *Las Meninas* (Velázquez), *The Third of May 1808* (Goya), *The Garden of Earthly Delights* (Bosch)  <br>**Tip:** Download the free audio guide and focus on the “Golden Triangle” (Velázquez, Goya, El Greco) to make the most of a 2‑hour visit. |
| **18:30 – 20:00** | **Sunset at Temple of Debod** (`temple-of-debod`) | • Ancient Egyptian temple with a spectacular sunset view over the city | **Address:** Calle de Ferraz, 28008 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 09:30‑13:30 & 16:00‑20:45 (seasonal)  <br>**Ticket:** Free  <br>**Tip:** Arrive 10 minutes before sunset for the best light; the site is a short walk from the Royal Palace. |

**Why it works:** All stops sit within a 2 km radius, so you can walk or hop on a quick metro ride. You get a balanced mix of royal history, iconic architecture, world‑class art, and a memorable sunset.

---

## 2️⃣ Art & Culture Loop – “Museums & Modern Madrid”

| Time (approx.) | Attraction | What to See / Do | API‑Provided Details |
|----------------|------------|------------------|----------------------|
| **09:30 – 12:00** | **Museo del Prado** (`prado-museum`) | Focus on the “Golden Triangle” collection (Velázquez, Goya, El Greco). | Same details as above. |
| **12:30 – 14:00** | **Museo Reina Sofía** (`reina-sofia-museum`) | • Picasso’s *Guernica* <br>• Works by Dalí, Miró, and other 20th‑century masters | **Address:** Calle de Santa María, 52, 28012 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 10:00‑21:00 (Mon‑Sat) / 10:00‑20:00 (Sun)  <br>**Ticket:** €10 (adult) – free after 19:00 on weekdays  <br>**Highlights:** *Guernica* (Picasso), *The Great Masturbation* (Dalí), *Woman from the Sea* (Miró)  <br>**Tip:** Grab a free map at the entrance; the rooftop café offers a great city view. |
| **14:30 – 15:30** | **Lunch – La Latina Tapas District** | Walk through Calle de la Cava Baja for classic tapas. | **Address:** La Latina, 28005 Madrid  <br>**Tip:** Try *patatas bravas* and a glass of vermú. |
| **16:00 – 18:00** | **Museo Thyssen‑Bornemisza** (`thyssen-bornemisza-museum`) | • European paintings from the 13th‑20th centuries, including Van Gogh, Monet, Caravaggio. | **Address:** Paseo del Prado, 8, 28014 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 10:00‑20:00 (Mon‑Sat) / 10:00‑19:00 (Sun)  <br>**Ticket:** €13 (adult) – free after 18:00 on weekdays  <br>**Highlights:** *Portrait of a Lady* (Van Gogh), *The Water Lily Pond* (Monet), *The Supper at Emmaus* (Caravaggio)  <br>**Tip:** Combine the ticket with the Prado (joint “Golden Triangle” pass) for €25 total. |
| **18:30 – 20:00** | **Evening Stroll – Gran Vía & “Madrilenian Lights”** | • Art‑deco architecture, street performers, iconic *Metropolis* building. | **Address:** Gran Vía, 28013 Madrid  <br>**Tip:** End the night at a rooftop bar (e.g., *Azotea del Círculo*) for a nightcap with city lights. |

**Why it works:** Perfect for art lovers who want to hit the three major museums in one day. All venues line the “Paseo del Prado” corridor, making transfers a 5‑10 minute walk. The evening finishes with the vibrant energy of Gran Vía.

---

## 3️⃣ Green & Scenic Madrid – “Parks, Views & Local Flavors”

| Time (approx.) | Attraction | What to See / Do | API‑Provided Details |
|----------------|------------|------------------|----------------------|
| **09:00 – 11:30** | **Parque del Retiro** (`retiro-park`) | • Crystal Palace, lake with rowboats, rose garden, statues. | **Address:** Plaza de la Independencia, 28011 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 06:00‑22:00 (free)  <br>**Ticket:** Free – boat rental €6 for 15 min  <br>**Highlights:** Crystal Palace, Lake, Rose Garden  <br>**Tip:** Rent a rowboat for a romantic paddle; it’s €6 for 15 minutes. |
| **12:00 – 13:30** | **Museo del Romanticismo** (small museum inside Retiro) | • 19th‑century paintings, period furniture, garden café. | **Address:** Calle de la Palma, 2, 28004 Madrid  <br>**Ticket:** €3 (adult) – free on Sundays after 14:00. |
| **14:00 – 15:30** | **Lunch – Mercado de la Paz (Chamberí)** | Fresh salads, Iberian ham, local cheeses. | **Address:** Calle de la Paz, 28010 Madrid  <br>**Tip:** Try the *tortilla de patatas* and a glass of Rioja. |
| **16:00 – 18:00** | **Teleférico de Madrid** (`madrid-cable-car`) | • 7 km aerial ride from Parque del Oeste to Casa de Campo; panoramic city views. | **Address:** Paseo del Pintor Rosales, 28008 Madrid  <br>**Opening:** 10:00‑22:00 (varies by season)  <br>**Ticket:** €6 (round‑trip)  <br>**Highlights:** Panoramic cityscape, ride over the Manzanares River  <br>**Tip:** Bring a light jacket; it can be breezy at altitude. |
| **18:30 – 20:00** | **Casa de Campo & Lake** (large urban park) | • Sunset walk around the lake, optional paddle‑boat, or a quick visit to the Madrid Zoo. | **Address:** Paseo de la Castellana, 28036 Madrid  <br>**Tip:** The park is free; the lake area is perfect for a picnic. |
| **20:30 – 22:00** | **Dinner – Taberna El Sur** (traditional tavern) | • Classic dishes: *cocido madrileño*, *churros con chocolate*. | **Address:** Calle de la Torrecilla del Leal, 28012 Madrid  <br>**Tip:** Arrive early; the place fills up quickly on weekends. |

**Why it works:** Highlights Madrid’s green lungs and offers spectacular aerial views. Ideal for families, nature lovers, or anyone who wants a relaxed pace with a dash of culture.

